---
title: Writer's notes vault — the one hook
---
%% Bard's vault has exactly one hook -- SessionStart -- and deliberately no
%% auto-commit, no periodic nudge, no per-prompt injection. GIT is reached by
%% a dashed, human-labelled edge rather than a hook arrow to make that
%% omission visible rather than silently absent.
flowchart TB
    classDef hook fill:#ffd8a8,stroke:#e8590c,color:#1e1e1e
    classDef vault fill:#d3f9d8,stroke:#2f9e44,color:#1e1e1e
    classDef session fill:#d0ebff,stroke:#1971c2,color:#1e1e1e
    classDef store fill:#e5dbff,stroke:#6741d9,color:#1e1e1e

    BEGIN["session begins"]
    H1["<b>SessionStart</b><br/>synapse-bard-hook session-start"]
    WORK["<b>Claude Code session</b><br/>writing, deciding"]

    IDX["Index.md"]
    FOLDERS["designs/ · tasks/ · ...<br/>plain notes, [[wikilinks]] anywhere in prose"]
    CLI["vault-search · vault-links<br/>backlink rank, wikilink resolution"]
    GIT[("the bible repo's own git history")]

    BEGIN --> H1
    IDX -->|"read"| H1
    H1 --> WORK
    WORK -->|"Read/Write/Edit directly"| FOLDERS
    WORK -->|"or via the CLI"| CLI
    CLI -.-> FOLDERS
    FOLDERS -.->|"a human commits --<br/>no auto-commit hook yet"| GIT

    class H1 hook
    class IDX,FOLDERS,CLI vault
    class BEGIN,WORK session
    class GIT store

    subgraph KEY["the colours"]
        direction LR
        K1["in the vault"]
        K2["the one hook"]
        K3["the session"]
    end
    class K1 vault
    class K2 hook
    class K3 session
    style KEY fill:#ffffff,stroke:#adb5bd,stroke-dasharray:4 4
